Lenses Bug Report: src/henchman/agents/working_memory.py\n## Date: 
2025-03-13T20:00:00Z\n## Bug Summary\nThe `should_read_file` method performs 
case-sensitive comparison `match.lines_read == "full"`, causing incorrect 
behavior when `lines_read` is "FULL", "Full", or any other case variation. Files
marked as fully read with non-lowercase "full" are incorrectly treated as having
invalid `lines_read` format, causing the system to think they need to be 
re-read.\n\n## Lens\n**Logic Gaps** - The code assumes a "happy path" where 
`lines_read` is always lowercase "full", but in reality, data could come from 
different sources (serialization, user input, etc.) with different casing.\n\n##
Expected vs. Observed\n| Expected Behavior | Observed Risk |\n|---|---|\n| When 
a file is marked as fully read (`lines_read` indicates full read regardless of 
case), any subsequent request to read any part of that file should return 
`False` (already read). | The code returns `True` with reason "Cannot determine 
overlap - invalid lines_read format" for case variations like "FULL", causing 
unnecessary file re-reads. |\n| The system should be robust to case variations 
in `lines_read` values. | The system is fragile and fails on case variations. 
|\n\n## Root Cause\n1. Line 236 in `should_read_file`: `if match.lines_read == 
"full":` performs exact string match.\n2. If `lines_read` is not exactly "full" 
(e.g., "FULL", "Full"), the check fails.\n3. The code then tries to parse it as 
a line range via `LineRange.from_str(match.lines_read)`, which returns `None` 
for "FULL".\n4. Finally, it returns `True, "Cannot determine overlap - invalid 
lines_read format"`.\n\n## Fix Plan\nChange the case-sensitive check 
`match.lines_read == "full"` to a case-insensitive check: 
`match.lines_read.lower() == "full"`.\n\n## Status: FIXED\n\n## Files 
Changed\n1. `src/henchman/agents/working_memory.py` - Line 257: Changed `if 
match.lines_read == "full":` to `if match.lines_read.lower() == "full":`\n2. 
`tests/agents/test_working_memory.py` - Added new test 
`test_memory_should_read_file_full_case_insensitive` to verify the fix and 
prevent regression.\n\n## Test Results\n- All 42 tests in 
`tests/agents/test_working_memory.py` pass\n- The new test 
`test_memory_should_read_file_full_case_insensitive` passes, confirming the fix 
works for both uppercase "FULL" and mixed case "Full"\n- Coverage improved: 
`src/henchman/agents/working_memory.py` now has 97% coverage (only 4 uncovered 
branches remain in other methods)'})
